  "prefLabel": "Ncr 563.03 Precautions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ncr 563.03 Precautions.\n\n(a) On all brush burning disposal areas, an attendant shall be on duty at all times until the fire is completely extinguished.\n\n(b) When a ban on open fires has been declared, brush disposal areas shall only be burned at times when fire protection is provided to keep the fire under control and keep from spreading, as determined by the forest fire warden or a forest ranger.\n\nSource. #14243, INTERIM, eff 4-23-25; ss by #14452 (formerly Ncr 5603.03), eff 12-6-25, EXPIRES 12-6-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ncr520-590.html"
